# Seed template for homelab/tle-dev/auth (Vault KV v2).
#
# Copy to .env.tle-dev-auth (gitignored, never committed) and fill what the
# ceremony did not generate: placeholders read `disabled` until replaced.
# Push with: ./seed-tle-dev-vault.sh
#
# Value forms:
#   KEY=literal            pushes the literal (no quotes needed; surrounding
#                          "double quotes" are stripped, so JSON is safe)
#   KEY=@relative/file     pushes the file's bytes (use for the PEM below;
#                          the file must also stay out of git)
#   empty / absent         key is skipped, Vault keeps its current value
#
# --- signing keys (product-issued, required) ---
# From the pinned TLE release (The-Last-Exam/server): the private half of
# the Ed25519 key whose public half is pinned as
# auth-jwt-ed25519-public-key-pem in ../../config/edge-config.yaml.
# Dev fallback: generate a pair locally and pin both halves together.
AUTH_JWT_ED25519_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM=@tle-dev-auth-jwt.pem
# Optional rotation staging key; leave empty until the #4 rotation flow.
AUTH_JWT_ED25519_STAGED_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM=
# --- OAuth providers (only the ones you enable; rest stay `disabled`) ---
# Apple / Discord / Google developer consoles, matching the client ids
# already in the TLE release's non-secret config.
APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
APPLE_CLIENT_SECRET_OVERRIDE=
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
